- *Standard JHipster Entities:**
- **User Entity** (Always present):

*   Fields: `id`, `login`, `passwordHash`, `firstName`, `lastName`, `email`, `activated`, `langKey`, `imageUrl`, `activationKey`, `resetKey`, `resetDate`

*   Managed by JHipster's user management system

- **Authority Entity** (Always present):

*   Fields: `name`

*   Defines user roles (e.g., ROLE_USER, ROLE_ADMIN)

- **Custom Entities** (Project-specific):

*   Defined in JDL files or through JHipster entity generator

*   Can have various field types: String, Integer, Long, BigDecimal, Boolean, LocalDate, Instant, etc.

*   Support for relationships: OneToOne, OneToMany, ManyToOne, ManyToMany

- *Standard API Endpoints:**
- *Authentication & User Management:**
- `/api/authenticate` - User login and JWT generation
- `/api/account` - Current user account management
- `/api/admin/users` - User administration (admin only)
- `/api/authorities` - Available authorities/roles
- *Actuator Endpoints (Management):**
- `/management/health` - Application health check
- `/management/info` - Application information
- `/management/metrics` - Application metrics
- `/management/configprops` - Configuration properties
- *Custom Entity Endpoints:**
- `/api/[entity-name]` - CRUD operations for custom entities
- Follows REST conventions (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE)
- *Development Commands:**
- *Backend:**
- `./mvnw` - Start backend server
- `./mvnw test` - Run backend unit tests
- `./mvnw verify` - Run all backend tests including integration tests
- `./mvnw spring-boot:run` - Start backend in development mode
- *Frontend:**
- `npm start` - Start frontend development server
- `npm test` - Run Jest unit tests
- `npm run e2e` - Run Cypress E2E tests (if enabled)
- `npm run lint` - Run ESLint
- `npm run prettier:format` - Format code with Prettier
- *Full Stack:**
- `npm run watch` - Start both frontend and backend in watch mode
- *Database:**
- `npm run docker:db:up` - Start database in Docker
- `npm run docker:db:down` - Stop database Docker container
- *JHipster Generator Commands:**
- `jhipster entity [EntityName]` - Generate new entity
- `jhipster` - Regenerate application
- `jhipster upgrade` - Upgrade JHipster version
- *Common JHipster Conventions:**
- REST controllers in `src/main/java/[package]/web/rest/`
- Services in `src/main/java/[package]/service/`
- Repositories in `src/main/java/[package]/repository/`
- Domain entities in `src/main/java/[package]/domain/`
- DTOs in `src/main/java/[package]/service/dto/`
- Frontend components follow feature-based organization
- Tests mirror the source code structure